B-3a (library ports) -- the fd calls the browser's libraries reach first:
fsync and fdatasync reach the kernel, the vectored calls move one record, and a
socket answers seeks, positional I/O and fstat as a socket.

fsync / fdatasync: 0001 parked __NR_fsync and __NR_fdatasync at the 0xFFFF
sentinel, so every ported program's fsync answered ENOSYS, though the kernel
has served SYS_FSYNC (55; fd, datasync) since the FS-mutation work. sqlite's
commit path fails SQLITE_IOERR_FSYNC on exactly this. Both now trap
SYS_FSYNC; a pouch socket fd answers EINVAL (nothing to synchronize, as POSIX
says and Linux answers for a socket), a vacant slot EBADF. The kernel's flat
-1 still decodes to EIO, so a handle without RIGHT_WRITE, a Dev with no fsync
(a pipe, the console) and a server error read alike.

readv / writev / preadv / pwritev: the kernel has no vectored I/O and the four
answered ENOSYS (0002 rewrote only stdio's backends around the absence). One
call per iovec would split a record the caller hands over whole -- a UDP
datagram, a pipe write within PIPE_BUF that POSIX makes atomic -- so
_pouch_iov.c gathers the vector into one buffer and moves it with one read or
write (the tag-aware wrappers, so a socket reaches its data handle), then
scatters a read back. Up to 4096 bytes ride the stack; more ride a heap buffer
of at most 1 MiB. A read moves at most one buffer (a short read). A write moves
the vector buffer by buffer and stops at the first short write or error,
answering the bytes written so far. A vector with one non-empty element moves
in place, without a copy. A cancelled thread's heap buffer is freed by a
cleanup handler. Validation is Linux's: count in [0, IOV_MAX], lengths summed
within SSIZE_MAX, else EINVAL; a positional offset that is negative or would
pass LLONG_MAX, EINVAL. A heap buffer that cannot be had answers ENOMEM.

lseek / pread / pwrite / fstat on a socket: a pouch socket fd is a libc slot
(0006, 0016), and these four handed its tagged number to the kernel, which
never issued it: EBADF, or EIO through the flat -1. Now a seek or positional
transfer answers ESPIPE (EBADF for a vacant slot), a negative pread/pwrite
offset EINVAL, and fstat a zeroed stat with S_IFSOCK | 0777, one link, and
the slot as its inode.

Not here, recorded: fcntl, dup and dup2/dup3 onto a number need the kernel's
POSIX dup and status-flag primitives, which today only the Linux phenotype
reaches; exposing them natively is a syscall addition (a vote). fsync on a
handle without RIGHT_WRITE fails where POSIX succeeds.

Device-side pin: usr/pouch-hello/pouch-hello-fd.c, census POUCH_CENSUS_FD.

